<ul>
<li>Fleet-wide margin <b>27.3%</b>; every vessel stays above 23% — no vessel goes into loss.</li>
<li>For the 3 largest vessels (WOORI, GOLDEN GRACE, ACE HANA), current actual billing already exceeds USD 6,500 — a real, visible price cut for the client, while margin remains healthy.</li>
<li>For the 2 smaller vessels (LUNA, MIR HANA), USD 6,500 is a modest increase over current actuals — balances the fleet and gives the client one predictable price.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Points to Note</h2>
<ul>
<li>Because the fee is flat, larger vessels earn a lower margin (~23.5%) than smaller vessels (~29%) — still profitable, but worth revisiting at next renewal.</li>
<li>The longer this decision takes, the higher the risk Hana Marine moves to NK or KR.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Requested Next Steps</h2>
<ol>
<li>Approve USD 6,500/vessel/year FYF.</li>
<li>Confirm our intent to pursue class on the newbuildings, so we can communicate this clearly to the client.</li>
</ol>

